    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dc9361ba-e1db-5bf3-94bf-ca86945d8fdd",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 27 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -23 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 34 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of $a_{21}=3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 27 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-9C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -23 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 34 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -23 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 34 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{2}:=C_{2}-9C_{1}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}-C_{1}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
