      ":question/id": "f40cc9b9-8546-59e9-bd0d-8943ba62aea3",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -10 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -49 & -43 & -9 \\\\ 12 & 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{13}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -10 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}+5C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 & 2 \\\\ -49 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 12 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -49 & -43 & -9 \\\\ 12 & 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{1}:=C_{1}+5C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{3}$.",
